#
#
#
# Spawn: south avenue, looking north up the street at the deck and the
# tower above the gate. Nothing is in melee reach on the first frame.
# --- pickups ---
# --- district B ---
#
# --- patrol graph (links are by NAME, so the graph survives reordering) ---
# Roof and deck get closed loops of their own: a street node must not
# link to a raised one, or the patrol line cuts through the stair.
#
# District B, ground loop.
# District B, high route: ring deck and tower top.
#
# --- encounters ---
# A. E1 crossroads: visible from the spawn at 16 units, newsstand cover.
# A. E2 east street: the substation guard.
# A. E3 relay hall: one behind a rack row, one on the far side.
# A. E4 gate approach.
# A. E5 deck and market roof, both seen from below first.
#
# B. E6 plaza: two in the open, one holding the gate itself.
# B. E7 promenade: the arcade is not free.
# B. E8 vault.
# B. E9 ring deck and tower top: the climb is contested.
#
# --- light ---
# Evening sun raking down the avenues from the west-north.
# Hall: cold strip lighting.
# Colonnade and deck.
# Market roof.
#
# B. Gate, plaza, promenade, vault, tower.
# Spine lamps: the tower's south face takes no sun, so the plaza needs
# its own light or the district reads as a silhouette.
#
# --- routing ---
# Two once-triggers, both clear of the spawn volume.
# Exit: the top of the relay tower. The destination spawn is
# Sektor_03_AegisBaseAlpha's authored playerstart (0 -46 0), just inside its
# south gate, so the base's gate-yard read survives the transition.

# ============================================================================
# Entities
